## 2026-11-01T09:30Z - Claude Opus 5.5 (as this session reports itself)
Corrections to the entry above - two of its claims were wrong:
- 31 ntcrun T-states: the fix was WRONG. The z80 module's frame_tick runs modulo its frame, 100000 T
  (_z80module.cpp: ticks_per_frame; frame_tick %= ticks_per_frame), so a step across a frame's end
  gave (small - big) & 0xFFFFFFFF, about 4 billion T. NTC's own regression didn't show it (nothing
  in it hangs on the clock); CyborgOS's did: cosregress's top and net_test failed (NET TEST timed
  GETs at -73846 ms), and both passed on the harness from before the change. Now step1 takes the
  difference modulo 100000. Checked: 30000 LD BC,nn steps through three frame ends count 10 T each
  (the one NOP at #FFFF 4); cosregress top and net_test pass; NTC's regression ALL PASS, 910 ok.
  Files: test/cpcrun.py.
- "GUI.CYB on the Next fails to compile (guiscr.joy)": FALSE - my warnings script ($S/coswarn.js)
  read the layout's consts as name=value only, and GUI.CYB/next's is a bare HEADZXN, so it compiled
  the wrong head. CyborgOS's builder builds it (build/gui/next/GUI.CYB). No CyborgOS bug.
  Files: none (the claim was in this log and the reply).


